    [v0.30.0][BugFix][Worker] Preserve PIECEWISE dummy query widths with DP and MTP (#18108)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Pick-from: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/18038
    
    With MRV2, DP and MTP enabled, an idle rank can fail in the draft model
    with `AssertionError: reusing a DP sync taken over a different batch`.
    PIECEWISE pads dummy model inputs while keeping the request count
    unchanged. Redistributing those padded tokens into dummy queries changes
    the uniform query width after the target model has synchronized it
    across DP ranks.
    
    Preserve the original dummy query token count with a context manager,
    pad the persistent model-input views, and match dummy attention metadata
    and slot mappings to those inputs. Restore the previous token count on
    normal completion and exceptions, including nested dummy runs.
    
    
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    N/A
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: jiajinzhu2 <jiajinzhu@huawei.com>

